{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'proposing|awaiting-grant|:lifted|:safepoint|step-export|successor' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc | tail -65; sed -n '25,43p' test/yin/vm/ucf/v2_support.cljc; sed -n '790,828p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/compose.cljc; sed -n '300,317p' collab/1791194000000-architect-m-next-d-plan-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md; rg -n '7.11.1|admission.*order' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf*; rg -n 'yin.k/successor|handoff|resumed' test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"8:   and its offer) and the exit half (the successor, the report, the\n26:   answers `:yin.k/awaiting-grant` for a valid version-1 blocked or\n31:   :proposing -- check the authority attachment (a missing one is\n35:   `:yin.k/awaiting-grant`; a grant to another, or an occurrence that\n72:   :safepoint -- the machine has nothing left to drive (halted, no wait\n92:   the driver answers the bytes (:lifted).\n98:   :safepoint under its own tenure.\n102:   successor's offer admitted.  :lifted and :aborted are the fork's and\n315:                        successor through `hand-off`)\n431:                              (contains? #{:yin.k/first :yin.k/successor :yin.k/result}\n1037:                 :phase :lifted\n1053:        (assoc :phase :proposing\n1061:        (with-status :yin.k/awaiting-grant\n1065:(defn- step-exporting\n1081:;; the successor append, the resumed report, the release, the closure\n1109:   automatic on a park).  The phase becomes :safepoint and the next\n1110:   step mints the successor; a machine that cannot enter exporting\n1115:    (let [{:keys [state refusal]} (arm-exit state :yin.k/successor)]\n1117:        (assoc state :phase :safepoint\n1125:  \"The first step of the exit: mint the successor occurrence once and\n1158:   send, naming the successor's address; for a halt the report carries\n1235:   continuation drives the successor's offer to its admission -- the\n1236:   last bracket -- so the successor is eligible exactly once.\"\n1245:              (or (some? (:yin.k/successor closed))\n1247:              (not= (:occurrence cell) (:yin.k/successor closed))))\n1256:                  {:yin.k/successor (:occurrence cell)\n1265:   fence, the successor append, the report, the release -- in order, so\n1275:      ;; the successor append: sent once before the report, per the\n1278:      (and (= :yin.k/successor (:role cell))\n1301:   successor an orphan and the exit over.\"\n1436:   `:yin.k/awaiting-grant`.  A minted id's intent record is durable in\n1486:          (with-status :yin.k/awaiting-grant\n1643:   closure, the expected interim answer of a successor's offer -- keeps\n1717:          (and (contains? #{:activating :running :safepoint} (:phase state))\n1834:(defn- step-proposing\n1962:            (not (contains? #{:running :safepoint} (:phase state))))\n2100:        (cond-> (assoc state :phase :safepoint)\n2199:              (assoc :phase :proposing :proposal nil)\n2200:              (with-status :yin.k/awaiting-grant\n2221:      ;; a valid blocked or parked root answers awaiting-grant at\n2223:      (= :yin.k/awaiting-grant (:yin.k/status r))\n2225:        (assoc state :phase :proposing\n2235:      (assoc state :phase :safepoint\n2267:                       (step-exporting state)))\n2268:        :proposing (if (= :program mode) state\n2269:                       (let [observed (step-proposing state)]\n2283:        (:running :safepoint) (step-active state mode)\n2323:         (not (contains? #{:stalled :failed :exited :aborted :lifted} (:phase state)))\n2324:         (or (and (= :proposing (:phase state))\n2338:                      (or (and (= :yin.k/successor (:role cell))\n2345:                          (and (= :yin.k/successor (:role cell))\n2492:   successor's journaled occurrence and prepared record are reused,\n2495:   rebuilt from the successor header's origin when no intent stands.\"\n2501:                  \"the successor's fenced record\" {})\n2518:                  \"the exit's report, from the successor's origin\" {})\n2572:    (if (and (= :proposing (:phase state)) (some? intent))\n2574:             :phase :proposing\n2595:   The fold decides which recovery runs: an exit whose successor is\n2611:                     (contains? #{:yin.k/successor :yin.k/result}\n2735:   outcome its append answered -- and a holder exporting a successor\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.handoff :as handoff]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]))\n\n\n(defn ring\n  [capacity]\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n                         ringbuffer/capacity-key capacity})))\n\n\n(defn make-ring-stream\n  [capacity]\n  (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n                       ringbuffer/capacity-key capacity}))\n\n\n\n\n(defn source\n  \"Add the source half: `config` carries :machine -- the machine at its\n   liftable safepoint, holding no custody -- beside the holder seams of\n   `holder` (no :bytes and :address: the driver mints those).  An\n   exclusive composition offers the export on its own arbitration --\n   the composition names it, and a supplied :arbitration is a refused\n   assembly; a fork composition (the composition's fork decision,\n   labelled :yin.k/fork) lifts without an occurrence, an offer or a\n   journal bracket, and the driver answers the bytes.  A source whose\n   progress journal already stands on the composition's substrate is\n   recovered by reopen, not re-exported: the machine matters only to a\n   first export.\"\n  [c h config]\n  (add-holder c h config driver/source))\n\n\n(defn restart\n  \"Recover holder `h` from its progress journal after a process\n   restart: a fresh handle over the same journal backend, folded by\n   `driver/reopen` -- a journaled grant never restores execution; it\n   releases and re-enters candidacy, and a complete fenced source\n   reopens fenced, resending its offer.  A stopped composition\n   reapplies the local stop latch: reopen never re-establishes it from\n   persisted state.\"\n  [c h]\n  (let [journal' (:dao.stream/handle\n                   (journal/open! (get-in c [:progress h :backend]) nil))\n        reopened (driver/reopen (assoc (get-in c [:holder-configs h])\n                                       :journal journal'))]\n    (-> c\n        (assoc-in [:progress h :journal] journal')\n        (assoc-in [:holders h] (if (:stopped? c)\n                                 (driver/stop reopened)\n                                 reopened)))))\n\n\n(defn journal-of\n- With the DHT store still hydrating, a renewal and a pending release are still sent.\n- The plain composition test has no `yin.repl` namespace loaded.\n- **(residual 4)** After `:running?` turns false, with a release held back by a full inbound stream: the control-plane step is called on every tick of the bounded drain, on each host's loop; the release is delivered once the stream accepts it; no program step runs.\n- **(residual 4)** With the stream full for the whole drain: the process exits within the existing budget, the release intent is in the journal, and a restart sends it.\n- **(residual 4)** `moved?` is true while a custody control-plane write is owed.\n\n**D16.**\n- Each corpus segment to each liftable row of 7.4.1, on both body versions, against the reference result and trace. Explicit park is checked through its parked record, not a pending. A held immediate is asserted to refuse.\n- 14.2.4 rows 1 to 5, 7 and 8 through the composition, same host; row 6's retry logic as a unit test.\n\n## 3. Boundary with E\n\n- **D owns** same-host driver and composition behavior on three lanes: protocol tests on the memory substrate, composition acceptance on a file-backed authority.\n- **E owns** the ordered cross-host pairs, real partitions and process kills, clause 10, the composition halves of clauses 3 and 8, and the per-host durability record.\n- **D hands E** `yin.vm.ucf.compose` as the only entry point, the regenerated fixtures, and the journal's record format.\n\n## 4. Risks, riskiest first\n\n328:    7.11.1; linker-dht 14.2.2 and 14.3 point to it. Its\n345:    applied them in 7.4.3, 7.7.8 and 7.11.1: checkpoint\n361:    7.11.1 and linker-dht 14.2.4 remain owed.\n388:    C12 sentences in 7.7.7 (enrollment retry), 7.11.1 (the stage-C\n484:;; The whole exclusive handoff, on a file-backed authority\n488:(deftest a-whole-exclusive-handoff-runs-on-a-file-backed-authority-test\n522:            (is (= 1 (count (inbound-requests (:inbound w) :yin.k/resumed)))\n523:                \"one resumed report, carried by the front\")\n527:                            (= :yin.k/resumed (:yin.k/action %)))\n548:            successor (get-in st [:detail :yin.k/successor])\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
