{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3096,3144p' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md; cat bb.edn | rg -n 'test:clj|build:yin-repl-node|test:cljs|test:cljd' -A8; rg -n 'keep|overflow|forg|attach' test/yin/vm/ucf/fencing_rows_test.cljc | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"8. Admission order and outcomes (7.7.8, 7.9). One fixture per check\n   in order: unreadable authority, wrong author, stale epoch, stale\n   lease, closed occurrence, a foreign id, an inherited id from a\n   closed ancestor, equal intent, different intent, fresh commit.\n   Add a cross-target conflict: one id sent to a second enrolled\n   target answers `:intent-conflict` from the shared namespace and\n   quarantines the occurrence. Add forged outcomes: a `:committed`\n   and an `:intent-conflict` from an unattributed author discharge\n   nothing and quarantine nothing. Add an unknown-effect transport\n   error, cut both before and after the remote commit: the id is\n   retained, the retry goes through the fenced boundary, and it\n   commits once or replays the result already held. Add an\n   unreadable accepted checkpoint: an inherited id answers\n   `:suspended` with tenure, quarantine, and dedup state unchanged,\n   and a stale holder still answers `:stale`. Add a snapshot\n   variant that keeps an id and changes its intent or the root\n   counter: the authority refuses it. Assert the exact\n   outcome map of 7.9 for each and that stale wins over an existing\n   record. Stage: C for the consumer, D for the driver.\n9. Bounds (7.7.8). A counter at 2^52-1 assigns nothing and refuses\n   export. An epoch at 2^52-1 is tested twice: while valid, its\n   grant activates and its effects commit; after the reclaim that\n   would increment it, the lapse is recorded, nothing is granted,\n   no successor is eligible, and admission answers `:suspended`\n   before tenure. The values 2^52 and -1 are refused on the bytes.\n   Stage: C for the epoch, D for the sequence.\n10. Composition (linker 14.2.4). The crash, partition, reclaim, and\n    successor-completion contracts run through the wired handoff\n    composition on both host matrices, with crash cuts around\n    completion and around result delivery. Stage: E.\n\nCanonical fixtures prove grammar parity. They do not prove\natomicity, attribution, or recovery; those need the durable\ntransactional seam of `yin.vm.linker.dht.md` 14.2.4.\n\n(M-next C, slice C12.) The stage-C gate proves the substrate: every\nauthority transition under every journal crash cut reopens to its\npre-state or its post-state with only whole transactions and a\nconverging retry, and one ledger's frames are byte-identical across\nhosts. It does not close clause 10: crash, partition, and\nsuccessor-completion through the wired composition, with real kills,\nremain stage E.\n\nNot claimed by this amendment, and still owed by the ownership row:\nexclusive custody itself, atomic admission, crash recovery, input\nreplay, and the `yin.repl.core` handoff composition. Governance\nrecovery, after quarantine, exhaustion, or lost authority state,\nstays outside the automatic protocol.\n6:  build:yin-repl-node\n7-  {:doc \"Compile the Node yin.repl (shadow-cljs build :yin-repl) to target/yin-repl.js\"\n8-   ;; yin.repl.dht-process-test spawns it as the JVM-to-Node reader of\n9-   ;; DHT epic S5, a required leg: a missing build fails that test.\n10-   :task (shell \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile yin-repl\")}\n11-\n12-  build:yin-repl-peer\n13-  {:doc \"Compile the yin.repl R5 cross-host peer (client role and --serve server role) as a Dart exe\"\n14-   ;; Process B of the R5 slice is a whole program rather than a test\n--\n20:   ;; and Node lanes, so `bb test` builds it first; a bare `bb test:clj` or\n21:   ;; `bb test:cljs` without it skips those tests with a printed notice\n22-   ;; rather than failing.\n23-   :task (do (shell \"mkdir -p build\")\n24-             (shell \"clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd compile yin.repl.slice-peer\")\n25-             (shell \"dart compile exe lib/cljd-out/yin/repl/slice-peer.dart -o build/yin-repl-peer\"))}\n26-\n27-  ;; Fast default lanes: no ^:slow test, no dao.test-slow/guard body.\n28:  test:clj {:doc \"JVM tests, fast: skips ^:slow ones; the DHT process test needs the Node REPL build\"\n29:            :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:python-antlr]\n30-            :task (shell \"clojure -M:test -e :slow\")}\n31-\n32:  test:cljs {:doc \"Node tests, fast: dao.test-slow guarded bodies print SKIP; needs the Node REPL build\"\n33:             :depends [build:yin-repl-node]\n34-             :task (shell \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test\")}\n35-\n36:  test:cljd {:doc \"Dart tests, fast: aggregated shards via src/dev/cljd_agg.clj; guarded bodies print SKIP\"\n37-             :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\n38-             :task (shell \"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\")}\n39-\n40-  ;; Every test, slow ones included (about 20+ minutes on the JVM).\n41-  test:all:clj {:doc \"Every JVM test, ^:slow included (20+ minutes); for unattended runs\"\n42:                :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:python-antlr]\n43-                :task (shell \"clojure -M:test\")}\n44-\n45-  test:all:cljs {:doc \"Every Node test, guarded slow bodies included (sets DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\n46:                 :depends [build:yin-repl-node]\n47-                 :task (shell {:extra-env {\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\" \"1\"}}\n48-                              \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test\")}\n49-\n50-  test:all:cljd {:doc \"Every Dart test, guarded slow bodies included (sets DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\n51-                 :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\n52-                 :task (shell {:extra-env {\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\" \"1\"}}\n53-                              \"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\")}\n54-\n--\n58:                 :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:python-antlr]\n59-                 :task (shell \"clojure -M:test -i :slow\")}\n60-\n61-  test:slow:cljs {:doc \"Node: only namespaces with dao.test-slow/guard, bodies enabled (DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\n62:                  :depends [build:yin-repl-node]\n63-                  :task (let [re (-> (shell {:out :string}\n64-                                            \"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --slow-regex\")\n65-                                     :out\n66-                                     clojure.string/trim)]\n67-                          (shell {:extra-env {\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\" \"1\"}}\n68-                                 \"clj\" \"-M:cljs\" \"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\"\n69-                                 \"compile\" \"test\" \"--config-merge\"\n70-                                 (str \"{:ns-regexp \\\"\" re \"\\\"}\")))}\n--\n84:        :depends [build:yin-repl-peer build:yin-repl-node test:clj test:cljs test:cljd]}\n85-\n86-  ;; Only the tests a change can affect (src/dev/affected.clj): the\n87-  ;; reverse require closure of the changed files since the merge-base\n88-  ;; with master. Extra args pass through (--base REF, --changed FILE...).\n89-  ;; Exit 2 on a wide change (deps.edn, bb.edn, src/dev/, ...): run bb test.\n90-  test:changed {:doc \"Fast tests a change can affect, three lanes in parallel\"\n91-                :task (System/exit\n92-                        (:exit (apply shell {:continue true}\n163:        [sref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 source)\n165:        [wref m3] (engine/attach-resource m2 target)]\n204:   prefix `p`.  Answers [outcome attaches].\"\n206:  (let [attaches (atom 0)\n207:        base (s/attacher (:t cp))\n208:        attach! (fn [d] (swap! attaches inc) (base d))\n211:            (s/new-machine :semantic {:attach-stream attach!})\n212:            (:bytes (:export cp)) attach!\n230:    [r @attaches]))\n399:        (is (zero? n3) \"nothing is attached\")))\n432:  \"An inbound appender whose acceptance is unknown, keeping each request.\"\n499:                (