{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_66","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='collab/1791377000000-compiler-engineer-ucf-d16final-gate.findings.md'\ns='''Completed-GMT: PENDING\nCompleted-Local: PENDING\nCoding-Agent: Codex (GPT-6)\n\n# D16-final audit and continuation — blocked, not accepted\n\nBranch \"'`ucf-d16-final`, HEAD `f6711518c2b8d8b4813f1ab50895409bffa3f88f`.\nNo git writes or production namespace edits were made. The requested gate is\n**incomplete**: two corrected completion-crash rows expose a landed production\nrecovery defect. This is not a report that D16-final passed.\n\n## Scope and inherited work\n\nRead the task brief, architecture/build guides, D-plan r3 D16 boundary,\nlinker 14.2.4, UCF 7.11.1 admission/composition contracts, D15a inbox and\nunavailable-inbox rulings, D14 recovery/exit-order ruling, driver-split ruling,\ncompose and the relevant holder recovery, export, writer, reader and evidence\npaths. Checked the partial tracked diff and untracked test files.\n\nThe interrupted session left more than the reported tracked diff:\n\n- `compose_test.cljc` exposed `log-writer`, `temp-dir`, and `cleanup-dir!`.\n  These are appropriate shared test fixtures; retained unchanged.\n- Untracked `compose_rows_test.cljc` already contained 19 candidate tests,\n  file-backed authority/progress/reply worlds, a reading/writing VM, held inbound\n  and journal-cut fixtures, regrant/replay/crash cases and exclusivity checks.\n  Its principal strength is driving `compose/open!`, source/holder addition,\n  control/program ticks, handoff and reopening rather than invoking holder\n  protocol operations directly. It reused the landed compose world and\n  portable lift/v2 helpers. The enrolled vs at-least-once target distinction,\n  stable-id replay assertions and fresh composition reconstruction were useful.\n- Untracked `zz_debug_test.cljc` was an exploratory test with no assertions.\n  Used temporary diagnostic traces while auditing, then removed that file.\n- Pre-existing untracked task brief and D-plan copy were left untouched.\n\n## Corrections made in the permitted test scope\n\n`test/yin/vm/ucf/compose_rows_test.cljc` now contains 20 tests:\n\n- Fixed 14 phase lookups that supplied `:phase` as `get-in`'\"'s default instead\n  of putting it in the path. These caused valid states to be stepped past\n  until the holder exited.\n- Fixed the nil-vs-nil replay-result comparison (\"'`:yin.k:result`), the zero-arg\n  predicate used by a one-argument drive, and proposal-answer inspection:\n  `:answered` is keyed by `[holder proposal-id]`, not maps in its values.\n- Retained the actual pre-eviction cursor when testing a retention gap.\n- Made the completion fixture hand off a still-parked continuation instead of\n  consuming its last input and accidentally creating a terminal result.\n- Made the successor-append cut match the successor occurrence, not the\n  source'\"'s earlier offer. Its uncommitted-report recovery checks regrant of\n  the last recorded origin checkpoint and successor ineligibility, consistent\n  with the D14 ruling. An acknowledged report need not be speculatively resent.\n- Used control-only scheduling for authored admission requests so guest\n  completion cannot race the fixture. Diagnosed wrong-author requests do not\n  receive replies. Separated stale binding checks from a quarantined world:\n  quarantine correctly suspends before tenure checks in the landed contract.\n- Restricted progress-frame cuts to positions 2–8, before activation, covering\n  both absent and persisted uncertain writes (14 combinations). Position 1\n  is journal creation/assembly, not driver recovery. Allowed an unminted fresh\n  export to remain non-runnable after the earliest absent cut.\n- Crash helpers close the actual composition at the cut. Formatted the tests;\n  fixed a transient unmatched delimiter introduced during fixture editing.\n\nNo production behavior was changed to make a row pass.\n\n## Blocking production defect: report survives, closure cannot complete\n\nBoth \"'`row-7-cut-after-the-resumed-report-test` and\n`row-7-cut-after-the-release-append-test` fail after a fresh file-backed\ncomposition/authority reopen. After 90 ticks the holder is still:\n\n```clojure\n{:phase :exiting\n :status :yin.k/ok\n :detail {:exit :yin.k/successor :step :closure}}\n```\n\nA separate bounded trace confirmed the ledger facts: the origin lease keeps\nits `:yin.k/result` body and `:yin.k/successor`, but its cause is `:policy`;\nthe origin occurrence advances to epoch 1, has no lease, and has no\n`:yin.k/closed` edge. The recovered release is authenticated/carried.\n\nThe landed paths explain the deadlock:\n\n1. `authority.grant/reopen!` reclaims every live lease with cause `:policy`\n   before handing out the authority.\n2. `ledger/closure-defect` permits closure only for a reported lease lapsed\n   with cause `:release` in that transaction.\n3. The recovered holder'\"'s carried release cannot supply that closure after\n   the policy reclaim; \"'`holder.driver/exit-closure-step` waits for the exact\n   origin lease/body/successor closure forever.\n\nThe composition exposes the necessary public driving/reopen operations;\nthere is no missing test accessor to work around. Repairing the recovery\ntransition requires changes to landed production logic and likely a ruling\non reported-lease reclaim semantics. Those namespaces are explicitly outside\nthis task'\"'s permitted diff. Stopped implementation at that boundary; kept\nboth red contract rows and did not bypass the policy reclaim, inject closure\nfacts, mutate holder state, or weaken the expected completion.\n\n## Whole-contract disposition and remaining work\n\n| Contract | Evidence now present | Remaining acceptance work |\n|---|---|---|\n| Row 1 | Two encodings, competing candidates, one grant, refusal and later regrant | Explicit competitor awaiting-grant cut; wakeable writer/direct-resume/install-child suppression |\n| Row 2 | Source remains fenced/parked until its own grant; later activation | Carrier/offer full, transport-error and unknown-acceptance cuts; abort restrictions and retained waits/ids after each phase |\n| Row 3 | Delayed old effect after reclaim is stale; current effect commits once and equal replay returns stored result | Explicit commit-before-reclaim alternative and two authored equal replays |\n| Row 4 | Before-commit and after-commit/before-result reopens; stored result replay; external side effect repeats | Broader unknown-effect boundary cuts and stronger explicit zero-at-cut/stable-id comparisons |\n| Row 5 | Kept cursor evicted; durable input replay vs missing-input re-read; authored divergent same-id intent conflicts and quarantines | Tie the divergence case directly to changed recovered input/intent, rather than authored boundary data |\n| Row 6 unit | Held request stream causes unchanged offer/proposal retries, one answer and one grant | Lost reply/lease-fact unit variants; this is not a real partition proof |\n| Row 7 | Before-report cut regrants last checkpoint; post-closure cut preserves closure and successor eligibility | Two post-report/release cuts are red production blockers; failure-lower and lost-authority cases still owed |\n| Row 8 | Unavailable authority, wrong author, stale epoch/lease, closure, foreign id, equal/different intent, fresh commit, quarantine | Full clause-8 fixture remains incomplete: inherited closed-ancestor id, cross-target conflict, forged outcomes, before/after unknown-effect transport errors, unreadable accepted checkpoint and counter/intent variants; exact outcome-map assertions and linker row-8 attachment/forgery/overflow/store-isolation cases |\n| Stage-D compose halves | Memory authority refusal, explicit fork label, fresh receiver recovery through progress-frame uncertainty | Actual content-store cuts around both stored objects, broader closure-bearing/alias/module/install recovery shapes and distinct program-IO counters |\n\nThe existing file-backed composition tests remain part of the focused run.\nThe D16-prep corpus/safepoint and fencing tests were not rewritten; the full\nJVM lane includes them. No same-host three-lane acceptance or stage-E\ncross-host/process-kill/partition durability claim is made. Fixture teardown\nfor newly added candidate backends also warrants a follow-up audit before\nlanding; not every inherited row records its latest composition in the\nouter world's cleanup value.\n\n## Test-first and validation evidence\n\nInitial run, before edits:\n\"'`clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.ucf.compose-test -n yin.vm.ucf.compose-rows-test`\nran **33 tests / 363 assertions / 47 failures / 4 errors**. This is observed\nred evidence for the inherited suite, not proof that the previous session\nfollowed TDD. Most failures were defective fixtures. Existing landed behavior\nneeds no invented production mutation to manufacture a red phase.\n\nCorrected focused run: **34 tests / 422 assertions / 4 failures / 0 errors**.\nAll four failures are the drive assertion and explicit `:exited` assertion in\neach of the two blocked row-7 tests. The genuine new recovery expectations\nremain red; there is no green implementation or completed TDD cycle for them.\n\nGREEN_SUBSET_PENDING\nFULL_JVM_PENDING\n\nChecks:\n\n- clj-kondo on both test files: **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\n- `cljstyle check` on both files: exit **0** after formatting one row file.\n- `git diff --check`: exit **0** (tracked helper diff; the untracked row file\n  was also checked by formatter/linter).\n- `bb test:clj` initially stopped before JVM tests: Node REPL build passed\n  (207 files, 206 compiled, 1 pre-existing namespace-clash warning), but the\n  pinned Python parser generation hit `UnresolvedAddressException` under the\n  sandbox. Babashka cleanup also reported a sandbox `sysctl` restriction.\n  Escalated `clojure -M:antlr-gen` then succeeded, generating four Java files\n  and classes in the ignored build directory. Ran the exact JVM fast test\n  command after those prerequisites, with escalation for process/socket tests.\n- Node and Dart test lanes **not run**: no landing or green acceptance claimed.\n\nChanged deliverables: shared compose-test helper visibility retained;\nnew/repaired compose row suite; removed inherited debug test; this requested\nfindings file. All implementation diff is under `test/yin/vm/ucf/`; this report\nis the explicitly requested exception under `collab/`. No git state writes.\n'\"'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ntail -8 /tmp/d16-jvm-fast-final.log; tail -8 /tmp/d16-green-rows.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
